e  length of the game or the flow of the  game at all I think the challenge is is  strictly the consistency which we look  at these plays that's going to be the  challenge in the bar which we officiate  these plays not on the field our  officials are doing that in real time  but the bar in which we look at these in  New York when they come to New York two  more things for you before I let you go  I know we've been talking a while but I  appreciate it so your comments to my  colleague Steve White's about hiring  coaches in sort of a copycat way looking  for the next Shawn McVeigh raised a few  eyebrows certainly since obviously you  were a young coach with an offensive  mind set a long time ago not too long  but that raised a few eyebrows d-did you  hear some of the blow back on that and  do you what are your well I think lost  years all the I saw the hit on Twitter  in the the challenge with that is you  really have to look at the whole  interview and the interview was really  about diversity in our hiring and look  it was a tough year for diversity when  you currently look at our general  managers 32 GM's in the league and and  our head coaches in the league and you  know that that has to be better there  there's some fantastic candidates so it  really wasn't directed at all at any one  of the new hires but the point being is  look it's hard enough to find the right  head coach fit in all of us understand  you know you really have three years to  prove yourself it's a you know it's a  we're changing coaches roughly at about  a 25 percent clip eight coaches a year  and and so history's told us those  successful head coaches don't have to  just come on offense I mean are you not  interested in the next Bill Belichick or  the next Tony Dungy I was trying to  reference the the overall the leadership  that we're looking for and and he takes  a guy like David Shaw who I worked with  the Eagles and he's doing a great job at  Stanford and he wants to stay in college  I thi